From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:17:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: sg-pc message box from the original Game.exe
 (SysMesBoxType.SGHD)

The STEINS;GATE (Steam) system message box (confirmations such as "Load this data?", "Exit Game?") as the original
draws and handles it, instead of the MO6TW box with estimated pieces and positions. Layout, art and behaviour come
from the original Game.exe: the box draw routine 0x43d470, the layout 0x43da50 (width, choice hit areas), the input
routine 0x43dc00, the SystemMes handler (0x464d00: two boxes, fades of 16 per frame) and the screen draw 0x46e650.

- New generic class UI::SGHD::SysMesBox + Profile::SGHD::SysMesBox (SysMesBoxType.SGHD): box pieces, text and
  choice positions, the highlight and the dimming are profile data.
- As the original: content width = the widest message, the choices with their spacing or a minimum; three DATA01
  pieces, the middle one stretched; messages left aligned with black copies up-left and down-right; choices right
  aligned on one row, the chosen one over a stretched highlight; no choice has the cursor at first, left / right wrap
  (from none to the first resp. last), Enter on none picks the first, Back moves the cursor to the second choice
  instead of closing, mouse / touch hover picks a choice and a click takes it.
- SystemMes: STEINS;GATE modes 10..17 are modes 0..7 of the native engine's second, global box (used by EXIT GAME);
  they were unknown modes, the string operands were not read and the thread crashed. They now open a separate box
  that dims the screen (black at 3 / 4 of its opacity) and reports its choice in SW_SYSSEL + 1, as the original
  (UI::SysMesBox gets a Global flag; only the SGHD instruction set uses it).
- sg-pc: hud/sysmesboxdisplay.lua rewritten for the new class.

Checked on MuMu (Android 15): "Load this data?" (load screen) and RETURN TITLE / EXIT GAME (system menu) show the
original layout (compared with a screenshot of the original), Enter picks then takes OK, Back moves to Cancel, a tap
on Cancel closes the box, EXIT GAME dims the screen and no longer crashes the script thread; mo6tw-pc-zhs title
unchanged.

